  "schema": 1,
  "note": "The published name data the linkage gate (docs/decisions/0010) reads, one entry per naming of the game and Minecraft version it exists for, each file pinned by SHA-256. A version with no entry has no name data, and no artifact is linked there. 'reads' says how an entry's inputs are read (srg-flat: Searge's joined.srg; tiny-flat: a Tiny v2 file; jar: the game's own class files in the names the artifact runs on; proguard-jar: an obfuscated game jar and Mojang's mappings), and 'owns' which classes the data speaks for: a reference to any other class is not the game's and is not checked. A namespace states 'reads' and 'owns' once and an entry may override them. 'resolve' says where myceliumRefreshNames finds a version's inputs; the build only ever reads the pins, which are fetched once into a cache and checked against them on every use. The repository check holds every entry to the version list and the era table.",
